    <p style="font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;color:#7A7268;margin:6px 0 0;">Your personal career agent</p>
  </div>
        </td>
      </tr></tbody></table>
      <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="width:600px;max-width:600px;"><tbody><tr>
    <td style="text-align:center;padding:20px 0 0;">
      <a href="https://test.charlie.local/unsubscribe?e=a%40b.com&amp;t=YUBiLmNvbQ.X5w3mqkoyLaqDgAqg-Cp2ycbq1rLRWpnf8CM-eLrL6k" style="font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;color:#AAA298;text-decoration:underline;">Unsubscribe</a>
    </td>
  </tr></tbody></table>
    </td>
  </tr></tbody></table>
</body>
</html>",
  "subject": "Has Lumora been in touch?",
  "text": "Hi Maya, your profile went to Lumora for the Senior Content Designer role. Has anybody from there contacted you yet?

If the answer is no, that is the normal answer this early and it is not a sign of anything. Hiring is slow in a way that has nothing to do with you. Sit tight.

If they do get in touch, at any point, I would like to know. A line is plenty.

I am asking because I genuinely cannot see it. I am not a job board. There is no tracker, no dashboard, and nobody feeding me updates from the inside. What I have is what you tell me, and I would rather ask you than guess.

If you would rather not, that is completely fine and I will not ask again.

Charlie",
}
`;

