    </tr><tr>
      <td style="width:16px;vertical-align:top;padding:0 0 9px;"><div style="width:5px;height:5px;border-radius:50%;background:#00B67A;margin-top:8px;"></div></td>
      <td style="font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.55;color:#4A453E;padding:0 0 9px;">How to position yourself for it, in your own words</td>
    </tr></tbody></table><p style="font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#4A453E;margin:0 0 14px;">One quick thing before I go deep: <b style="color:#2A2521;font-weight:600;">what's your pay floor?</b> Just reply, that's the whole reply.</p><p style="font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.62;color:#4A453E;margin:0 0 14px;">This stays a conversation. Change what you're after any time, just reply. And if you've got more that shows your work, a deck, a case study, a writeup, send it over and I'll fold it into what I look for.</p>
          <div style="margin:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #ECE9E3;padding:16px 0 0;">
