  "subject": "A few things I am missing about you",
  "text": "Hi Maya, when I put you in front of a company, I can only hand over what you have actually given me. Anything I do not have I either leave out or I fill in myself, and a guess about you is worse than a blank.

Here is what I cannot answer for you right now:

- A link to your work. A portfolio, a site, case studies, a deck. Anything I can open.
- What you are expecting on pay.
- How soon you could start, counting your notice.
- One piece of work you are proud of, in your own words. What it was, what you did, and what changed because of it.
- What you actually want next. The kind of company, where you want to be based, and the work itself.

One reply with whatever you have is plenty, and partial is fine. If something on that list is none of my business, say so and I will stop asking for it.

There is nothing to apply to here and this is not about one job. It is so that when something does fit you, I am working from your words.

Nothing with your name on it goes to any company until you tell me it can.

Charlie",
}
