  "subject": "A product manager role in Pune, and why I thought of you",
  "text": "Hi.

You told me I could send you roles beyond the one you came to me for. This is one of those.

A software company in Pune is hiring a product manager.

I thought of you because you have owned a product from discovery to launch. That is from your own answers, not a guess of mine.

Three questions, and short answers are fine:

1. Are you looking at the moment?
2. Does this role interest you?
3. If yes to both, may I take the next step with you?

The next step is not your name going to them. They have set a high bar on the products you have shipped, so I would come back with three specific questions first. I only put someone forward when I can back them with their own work, and I will tell you straight if I cannot.

I am not naming the company in this email. You will know exactly who it is before your name goes anywhere near them, and you can stop at that point.

If it is a no, say so and that is the end of it. If I do not hear back, nothing happens and nothing is held against you.

Charlie",
}
`;

